  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.5.0\n\n      New Features:\n      - EMV TLV support: new NetCore8583.Tlv namespace with full BER-TLV parsing, building, and ISO 8583 field integration.\n      - TlvParser: parses BER-TLV encoded byte data into TlvTag records, handling single-byte tags, multi-byte tags (2–3+ bytes), and multi-byte lengths (definite form).\n      - TlvBuilder: fluent API for constructing BER-TLV encoded byte sequences with .AddTag(tag, value).Build().\n      - TlvTag: immutable record type with Tag (hex string), Length, Value (byte[]), Description, nested tag support for constructed data objects.\n      - EmvTags: built-in frozen dictionary of common EMV tag descriptions (9F26, 9F27, 9F10, 9F37, 9F36, 95, 9A, 9C, 5F2A, 82, 9F1A, 9F03, 9F33, 9F34, 9F35, 9F09, 84, and more).\n      - TlvField: ICustomBinaryField implementation for registering field 55 (or any TLV field) as a TLV-aware composite field.\n      - IsoMessage TLV extensions: GetTlvTags(), SetTlvTags(), GetTlvBytes(), FindTlvTag() helpers for convenient field 55 access.\n\n      v2.4.0\n\n      New Features:\n      - Fluent MessageFactoryBuilder API for code-first configuration without XML. Supports headers, templates with inheritance, parse maps with inheritance and exclusion, composite fields, custom fields, and all factory properties.\n\n      Performance:\n      - Bitmap128 struct backed by UInt128 replaces BitArray for field-presence tracking with zero heap allocations.\n      - Span and ReadOnlySpan used throughout parsing and encoding for zero-copy byte/string conversions.\n      - Zero-copy byte utilities via MemoryMarshal.Cast; Stringx extensions encode directly into destination buffers.\n      - EncodingCache and ArrayPool pooled variants reduce allocations on hot paths.\n      - All parsers, IsoMessage, IsoValue, MessageFactory, and codecs updated to use span-based APIs.\n\n      Breaking Changes:\n      - NetCore8583.Util namespace reorganised into NetCore8583.Extensions. Update using statements if you reference HexCodec, Bcd, Arrays, OsUtil, or other utilities directly.\n      - Removed: ByteUtil, DateUtil, StringUtil from NetCore8583.Util (replaced by equivalents in NetCore8583.Extensions).",
